<title>SWEDEN: Handelsbanken posts 14 pct rise Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Handelsbanken posts 14 pct rise Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's largest bank Handelsbanken on Monday posted its results for the first three months of 1997 ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profits			1,727  vs  1,517</p>
<p> Credit losses				136  vs    449</p>
<p> Net interest income		    2,607  vs  2,230</p>
<p> Earnings/share (Crowns)		 5.62  vs  4.93</p>
<p> Net commission				797 vs    673</p>
<p> Net financial items			   6 vs    492</p>
<p> Other operating income		    159 vs    117</p>
<p> Total income				3,575 vs  3,517</p>
<p> Total costs				 1,712 vs  1,551</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     1,863 vs  1,966</p>
<p> Tax					     524 vs    388</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,344 vs  1,173</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll found analysts expected Handelsbanken to post a profit after credit losses of 1.64 billion crowns for the first quarter.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
